From 1bc0f9e0203b31dcb7da63116f5f670217a7cc0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed <ahmedmh03.work@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:02:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(order-service): require an Idempotency-Key on POST
 /orders

A client that times out can't tell whether its order was saved, so it retries and
gets a second order. The key is claimed in the same transaction as the order
(unique customer_id + key), so a retry or a double click returns the original order.
Same key with a different request is a 422; a retry still works while inventory is down.
